<div class="meta">Lesson 0016 · Rendering · from issue #64 (plaza fountain)</div>
<h1>Composite Modeling from Primitives</h1>
<p>Asset packs never cover everything. When the missing piece is simple
enough, the cheapest fix is to <em>compose</em> it from the primitives your
renderer already ships — no new downloads, no modeling tool, no license
review.</p>

<h2>The gap</h2>
<p>The downtown map authors a <code>fountain</code> obstacle: an 8×8 collision
AABB in the park. The KayKit City Builder pack has buildings, cars, and
benches — but no fountain. The stand-in (the pack's flat <code>base</code>
tile) satisfied the renderer but read as a pancake, not a landmark.</p>

<h2>The technique</h2>
<p>A fountain is geometrically boring: stacked cylinders. raylib's immediate-
mode primitives (<code>DrawCylinder</code>, <code>DrawCylinderWires</code>)
can build one in ~10 draw calls:</p>
<pre><code>basin wall   DrawCylinder(r=R,      h=25% of height)  stone
basin water  DrawCylinder(r=0.88R,  h=0.03)           translucent blue
column       DrawCylinder(r=0.18R→0.26R, h=50%)       stone (tapered)
upper bowl   DrawCylinder(r=0.45R,  h=15%)            stone
bowl water   DrawCylinder(r=0.38R,  h=0.03)           translucent blue
finial       DrawCylinder(r=0.07R→0.14R, h=25%)       dark stone</code></pre>
<p>Two rules made it fit this codebase instead of fighting it:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Size from the contract, not constants.</strong> Total height comes
from the fountain's <code>SizeSpec</code> table entry; radii derive from the
authored collision AABB. Visuals and collider match by construction — the
same single-sourcing rule every model follows.</li>
<li><strong>Dispatch before the fallback.</strong>
<code>Assets::modelForBuilding</code> maps <em>uncurated</em> ids to a hashed
generic building so filler blocks always render. Deleting the curated
<code>fountain → base</code> entry alone would have summoned a random
skyscraper in the park. The composite is dispatched by id <em>before</em> the
model lookup.</li>
</ul>

<h2>The two bugs screenshots caught</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Cause</th><th>Fix</th></tr>
<tr><td>Fountain reads as a flat platform</td><td>SizeSpec height 1.2 was
tuned for the old pancake tile; on an 8-unit footprint the proportions say
"stage", not "fountain"</td><td>Raise the table value to 2.6 — sizing stays
table-driven</td></tr>
<tr><td>Basin water invisible</td><td><code>DrawCylinder</code> renders a
<em>capped solid</em>; the basin's own stone top hid the recessed water disc
inside it</td><td>Float each water disc as a thin (0.03) cylinder just
<em>above</em> its stone cap</td></tr>
</table>

<div class="callout warn"><strong>Capped-solid gotcha.</strong> Immediate-mode
"cylinder" in most APIs is a closed solid, not a tube. Anything you nest
inside one is invisible from above. Either float the inner surface above the
cap, or build walls from ring segments.</div>

<div class="callout good"><strong>When to compose vs. when to import.</strong>
Compose when the object is a landmark silhouette made of ≤ a dozen convex
chunks (fountains, pillars, planters). Import when it needs texture detail,
concavity, or animation — a composite car would look like soap bars.</div>

<h2>Why this matters again later</h2>
<p>The same pattern covers any future pack gap (statue, flagpole, fireplug
variants), and the same <em>dispatch-before-fallback</em> shape appears
anywhere a lookup has a default: check the special case before the map, or
the default silently swallows it.</p>
